    "body": "## Overview\n\nA non-streaming background `/v1/responses` request whose generation raises stays `\"queued\"` forever. `_run_background_request` only marks the stored response `\"failed\"` when `responses_full_generator` returns an `ErrorResponse`. Exceptions from the engine generator propagate instead, for example `VLLMValidationError` for `top_logprobs` above `--max-logprobs`, or `GenerationError` for `finish_reason=\"error\"`. Nothing awaits the background task, so the error is dropped, and clients polling `GET /v1/responses/{id}` never see a terminal status. This catches the exception, logs it, and marks the response `\"failed\"`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- A background request whose generation raises now ends with `status=\"failed\"` instead of `\"queued\"`.\n- The exception is logged with its traceback rather than lost in an unawaited task.\n- No change for successful requests, `ErrorResponse` returns, or cancelled responses (`\"completed\"`/`\"cancelled\"` are still preserved).\n\n## Validation\n\nReal server on `34ac4f96a3` (Qwen3-0.6B, RTX 4090, `--enforce-eager`, `VLLM_ENABLE_RESPONSES_API_STORE=1`, default `--max-logprobs 20`). Request: `{\"input\": \"Say hi.\", \"max_output_tokens\": 8, \"top_logprobs\": 50, \"include\": [\"message.output_text.logprobs\"]}`.\n\n| Build | Foreground | Background `POST` | Background `GET` after 5s |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `main` | HTTP 400 `Requested sample logprobs of 50, which is greater than max allowed: 20` | 200 `queued` | 200 `queued` (never changes) |\n| this PR | same | 200 `queued` | 200 `failed` |\n\nTests:\n\n- New `tests/entrypoints/openai/responses/test_serving_responses.py::test_background_request_fails_when_generation_raises`. It fails on `main` with the escaped `VLLMValidationError` and passes with this PR.\n- `pytest tests/entrypoints/openai/responses/test_serving_responses.py`: 67 passed, 1 xfailed.\n- `pre-commit run --files <changed files>`: all hooks pass.\n\n## Details\n\nThis PR only touches the non-streaming background path. The streaming background path (`_run_background_request_stream`) has a related hang on producer errors, which #49721 addresses, so I left it alone to avoid conflicts.\n\nNot a duplicate: I found no issue or PR for this (searched \"responses background\", \"background response failed\", \"_run_background_request\"). #49721 changes the streaming background consumer. #38190 (draft) wraps `create_responses` to return a `response.failed` event, but does not touch the background task. #62549 is about streaming retrieval with no stored events.\n\nAI assistance was used to find this bug, write the fix and the test, and run the validation shown above.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
